        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5e09093972e34da1be52d0380a436c7e",
      "statement": "The conditional-write store is built with retries off: a retried CAS put can land on the first attempt's own token change and report a clean 412, converting 'may have committed' into a false rejection, so the ambiguity must surface as Err for the caller to reconcile.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/bucket.rs#L155-L159",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:55966316b6e34f7d770501c27990c9a4c0f31e2395636900e25a4bf0e8a181a4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_06527debdf8b4b1ca43d5b4a0fe707c8",
      "statement": "split_spec splits a [s3://|gs://|az://]NAME[/PREFIX] value into backend, bucket name, and a slash-terminated key prefix; a spec without a scheme stays S3-compatible, a spec without a prefix keeps keys at the bucket root, and on az:// the NAME is the container with the account from AZURE_STORAGE_ACCOUNT_NAME.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/bucket.rs#L190-L214",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:146023f29e833424cdee2c5f11c1744a70441472ca6e0cca958aee765633bec9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_13972663aee947bd9331dee5743e6842",
      "statement": "There are two conditional-write dialects: S3 and Azure Blob Storage use the etag as If-Match / If-None-Match, Google Cloud Storage uses the object generation as x-goog-if-generation-match; is_clean_cas_rejection treats Precondition and AlreadyExists as clean rejections and every other error as ambiguous because an ambiguous write can have changed the object.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/bucket.rs#L178-L188",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b41d72fa34a9d07d5a8d52d40a3f82035b7cd36e2ba57534c17b6a54a81b7ef6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/bucket.rs#L67-L137",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c528e144a6d911821a319e946a96a1a50fe8ca0cf72a0b8a8a3b73076c9f0958:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c1a143a4f36949f6a6271f0659c6723e",
      "statement": "The bucket must provide a conditional create, a conditional overwrite, and read-after-write consistency; the qualified stores are Amazon S3, Cloudflare R2, Tigris, Google Cloud Storage, and Azure Blob Storage, while Backblaze B2, Hetzner, and DigitalOcean Spaces do not implement the required conditional writes and MinIO community edition is not qualified for production.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L16-L41",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6f70c947292aa75c47238dc590a1a78f335f32f0d65322d993cd144077e37894:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1f1a2bc1ad2042838441841c0daeeca8",
      "statement": "Every node tests the store's conditional-write contract once at startup (two of four probe writes must fail) and stops on a broken store; CELLD_STORAGE_PROBE=0 disables the test, and celld reserves the probe/, cells/, nodes/, node-cells/, fleet/, deploy/, deploy-blobs/, wake/, and telemetry/ key prefixes.",
