          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/local_store.rs#L1-L10",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f4a4fff22e1eb1d7702bf98de41883b26ed888a072a013c010381d4e01c4dc29:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_00d6c478cd41492a9f045f28c268f8f1",
      "statement": "Credential handling is per provider: S3-compatible buckets use the standard AWS credential chain, gs:// buckets use Application Default Credentials and reject an S3 --endpoint, and az:// buckets require exactly one credential family (account key, managed identity, or AKS workload identity) with the authority host restricted to the public Azure cloud; AZURE_STORAGE_USE_EMULATOR selects Azurite for development only.",
